<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps upgrades Province of Mendoza rating.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps upgrades Province of Mendoza rating.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Friday it upgraded the foreign currency rating for the Province of Mendoza to double-B from double-B-minus.</p>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps said Mendoza's foreign currency debt rating is now on par with that of the Republic of Argentina.</p>
<p>Mendoza's debt burden of about $981.6 million consists primarily of bank loans and other obligations, which financed the recapitalization and clean up for privatization of the province-owned banks.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
